diff --git a/src/interpreter/wrapped-paragraphs.md b/src/interpreter/wrapped-paragraphs.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c73502a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/interpreter/wrapped-paragraphs.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Wrapped Paragraphs
+
+A Markdown file kept the way these are wraps its paragraphs
+at eighty columns, so each line ends
+with a word that
+the next begins. The
+reader joins them
+with a space, as a browser does, rather than running them together into one.
+
+This paragraph wraps
+with *emphasis at*
+*the edge* and a link
+[near the end](https://example.com). A hard
+break  
+starts a new line without a space at its start.
